Subject: [PATCH] slice-ws2812: terminate DMA before releasing the channel

ws2812_remove() releases the DMA channel without first ensuring any
in-flight transfer is stopped. Under module reload / device teardown
this can race with an active DMA transfer and crash. Call
dmaengine_terminate_sync() before dma_release_channel() to make
teardown safe.

diff --git a/ws2812.c b/ws2812.c
--- a/ws2812.c
+++ b/ws2812.c
@@ -521,6 +521,7 @@ static void ws2812_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	if (state->dma_chan)
 	{
+		dmaengine_terminate_sync(state->dma_chan);
 		dma_release_channel(state->dma_chan);	
 	}
 
